// AUTO-GENERATED from CRESTA_2019_Zoning_Schemes.xlsx (PERILS CRESTA AG, 2019 release).
// Source spreadsheet is a coverage catalog: it lists, per country, the available CRESTA
// zoning schemes (zone counts, scheme type, and one example zone code per resolution).
// It does NOT contain zone boundary geometry — the licensed PERILS CRESTA shapefile/GeoJSON
// dataset must be supplied separately and loaded into the `geometry` column for zones to
// render on the map. Until then each seed row carries `geometry: null` and the map layer
// simply renders nothing for that zone (the toggle and plumbing still work end-to-end).
//
// `code`       — CRESTA zone code (e.g. "AFG_BAL"). Example codes come straight from the sheet.
// `resolution` — 'low' (Low-Res scheme) | 'high' (High-Res scheme).
// `scheme`     — the administrative scheme the zone belongs to (e.g. "Province").
// `zoneCount`  — total number of zones in that country's scheme (for the coverage legend).
// `geometry`   — GeoJSON Polygon/MultiPolygon once the boundary dataset is loaded; null for now.

